analysisWe need to produce assert statement for the comment.

We have method remove(Object o). The comment: "If the queue initially contains the specified element, then the size of the queue after removal is one less than the initial size."

We need to refer to old size before removal, and after removal size via this.size() or size() method. The method returns boolean indicating if element was present and removed. The specification: If initially contains the specified element, then after removal size = old size - 1. So we need to condition on old contains(o). Use \old(this.contains(o)). Also need to express size after removal: this.size() (or this.size()? size method returns int). Use this.size().

Thus assert: \old(this.contains(o)) => this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1;

But also need to ensure that if not contains, size unchanged? Not required by comment. Only conditional.

Thus final answer: <code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1;</code>

Check syntax: Use parentheses maybe: assert (\old(this.contains(o)) => this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1); but they often omit outer parentheses. In examples they used assert (\old(this.contains(value)) => ...) && ... So we can include parentheses to be safe.

Thus final.assistantfinal<code>assert (\old(this.contains(o)) => this.size() == \old(this.size()) - 1);</code>
